{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>He, the one in charge over the land, he is the one distributing grain.</b> Despite being the one in charge, he himself was the seller, and he did not trust his servants — for the silver was very abundant and rightfully belonged to Pharaoh, as it says: וַיָּבֵא יוֹסֵף אֶת הַכֶּסֶף בֵּיתָה פַרְעֹה (Genesis 47:14). Therefore no grain was sold to buyers without his seal or handwritten signature." "<b>And Joseph's brothers came and bowed down to him.</b> And since, despite being the one in charge, he himself was the one distributing grain, Joseph's brothers were required to come directly to him and not speak to his servants alone."], :book :genesis, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 42, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:34:15.918546355Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}